WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.137
-Bill, I want to ask.
You have three lovely daughters.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.638
Are they fans of your work?

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:09.642
Have they engaged with anything
you've done yet?

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.246
-Well, they know me from,
like, a lot of animated movies

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.915
like "Inside Out" and "Cloudy
with a Chance of Meatballs."

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:20.219
I did show them a couple of --
they wanted to, you know --

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:23.589
I had the thing where, you know,
my oldest came in -- she's 11 --

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:27.160
and said, "Hey, kids at school
said you were on a show

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.896
called 'Saturday Night Live,'"
and I go, "Yeah."

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:35.501
So I showed her
and her sister Harper the --

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:36.869
I was like,
"What do I show them?"

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:38.871
And I ended up showing them
the puppet sketch,

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:42.508
where I was the puppet --
-Fantastic.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.577
-And they thought
that was funny.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.712
And then I showed them
the one where I, again,

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:49.515
another John Solomon,
Rob Klein sketch

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:52.184
where I was kind of
this effeminate firefighter.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:55.121
-[ Laughs ] It's one of
my favorites, with Adam Levine.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.557
-Adam Levine, yeah, and it was
called "The Firehouse Incident."

00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:01.927
And they were
really confused by that.

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:04.564
And then I watched --
and then I showed them Stefon,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.199
and my oldest,
after the third one went,

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:08.468
"Do you laugh in all of these?"

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.469
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:11.771
Yeah, yeah, I do.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.474
And she goes -- I go,
"But my friend John Mulaney,

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.842
he was writing stuff
I hadn't seen."

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.378
And she was like, "Alright."

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.979
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:23.550
-I think about the firefighter
sketch more than maybe anybody

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.853
because your character finds out

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.289
that they canceled
a television show.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.823
"Don't Tell the --" What was it?

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.860
"Don't Tell --"
-Uh...

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.428
-"Don't Tell the Bee
in Apartment --"

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.230
-23.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.831
-Bobby Moynihan walks in
and goes, "Did you hear

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:41.334
they canceled
'The Bee in Apartment 23'?"

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.137
And I go, "What?!"

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:47.005
-You go,
"They canceled the bee?!"

00:01:47.005 --> 00:01:48.708
-"Canceled the bee?!"

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.344
And then I think I say, "Open
that window because I want to

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.913
throw a dog out the window,"
and everybody goes, "No!"

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.983
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.617
-And your kids thought
that was weird?

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:01.387
Hey --
-They weren't into it.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:04.790
And I blew my voice out
doing it, I remember.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.994
-We do talk about Second Chance
Theater a lot of this show.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:11.898
And I believe "Song for Daddy,"
was that also Klein and Solomon?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.399
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:17.203
We're just talking about John
Solomon and Rob Klein sketches,

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.604
which were amazing, but, yeah,

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:21.241
"Song for Daddy"
was Justin Bieber.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:26.146
And that sketch
only went to dress,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.514
and everything that could
possibly go wrong

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:31.084
in a sketch went wrong
during that sketch.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:35.154
Immediately I think the set
almost fell on Justin Bieber.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.690
-Right.
-And then I tried to make it,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.292
like, a part of the sketch
or something.

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:42.761
And then I remember
none of the props

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:45.031
I was supposed to have
were there.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:49.902
And it went --
it just went terrible.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.638
And then at the end, I remember
Kenan Thompson came in

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:55.374
as Steve Harvey, and he went,
"I don't know. I like it."

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:57.509
And it was almost like he was
talking about the sketch.

00:02:57.509 --> 00:03:00.146
[ Laughs ]

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.848
But I can remember --
My favorite memory of that

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:05.018
was going upstairs after it
happened and going up to

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:08.821
the writers room on nine,
still in my costume,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:12.691
and walking into the
writers room on the ninth floor

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:16.362
and James Anderson
just on the floor, laughing,

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.364
and he tackled me
and started laughing

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.566
because it was, like, this --

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:23.169
Everybody was just like,
"That was..."

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.905
-Yeah.
-That was one of the classic,

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.506
like, everything
that could go wrong --

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:30.276
I think it's online someplace,
but it just ate it.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:33.846
-It was also -- It was,
like, height of Bieber fever.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.549
And I think in those days,
probably now too,

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.452
when you have dress rehearsals,
sometimes that's when I feel

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:42.488
like NBC executives, like,
pull tickets for their kids.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:45.458
And so it was a way younger
crowd, and they were just there

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.493
because they loved him,
and the sketch started,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.663
and immediately the set almost
fell on him and people gasped.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:55.568
-I'm an old, grizzled cowboy
singing a song about his daddy,

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.236
and I remember getting up there
and seeing the crowd,

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.004
and Fred Armisen
was playing the drummer.

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:02.041
And Fred was like, "There's a
lot of, like, young kids here."

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.242
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:05.711
And I was just like,
"Oh, we're screwed.

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.012
This isn't going to play."

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:10.149
And just seeing John Solomon
just in the audience,

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:13.386
pleasantly looking at me, going
like -- just knowing like --

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:16.622
I was in front of
a firing squad, you know.

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:20.225
-It was -- We'll do it here
one day and we'll just have

00:04:20.225 --> 00:04:22.595
a grizzled audience
full of cowboys for you.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:25.231
Just like old --
Because that's who it was for.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.733
-That's who it was for. Yeah.

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:29.134
-Buddy, thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:29.134 --> 00:04:32.071
It is always such a joy
and a pleasure to see your face.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.073
-You too, pal.
-I'll see you soon.

